1
00:00:03,450 --> 00:00:07,113
A question may need a direct answer, dependent tasks, or a
tool.

2
00:00:07,293 --> 00:00:11,003
DynaAgent lets a coordinator construct that workflow at
runtime.

3
00:00:11,183 --> 00:00:15,088
Its agents are roles and tool selections around an
external model.

4
00:00:16,333 --> 00:00:18,224
Here is the complete architecture.

5
00:00:18,404 --> 00:00:24,985
The command line or Streamlit sends context to a
coordinator, which defines workers and a dependency graph.

6
00:00:25,165 --> 00:00:29,585
Ready workers execute, optionally vote, and pass results
to a reviewer.

7
00:00:29,765 --> 00:00:35,588
Review returns an answer or schedules follow up tasks;
simple questions can return directly.

8
00:00:35,768 --> 00:00:42,067
SQLite retains successful plans and tool code, while
recent conversation stays in session memory.

9
00:00:42,247 --> 00:00:48,211
Every model role uses the Responses client, under a shared
budget, with tools invoked as needed.

10
00:00:49,450 --> 00:00:51,968
Each task declares dependencies and a worker.

11
00:00:52,148 --> 00:00:55,022
The graph links task outputs to the tasks that need them.

12
00:00:55,202 --> 00:00:59,678
Independent tasks run concurrently, and the scheduler
records their outputs.

13
00:00:59,858 --> 00:01:05,711
A dependent task becomes ready when all its dependencies
finish, using their outputs as context.

14
00:01:06,950 --> 00:01:10,501
A worker combines a role, instructions, and selected
tools.

15
00:01:10,681 --> 00:01:14,295
Its prompt brings together the question and dependency
outputs.

16
00:01:14,475 --> 00:01:18,113
Matching agent names reuse the persona and merge tool
sets.

17
00:01:18,293 --> 00:01:21,992
The Responses client sends the request to the configured
model.

18
00:01:23,233 --> 00:01:26,665
Workers can use a calculator or provider hosted search.

19
00:01:26,845 --> 00:01:32,884
For a new tool, the coordinator generates a Python
function, checks its definition, and registers it.

20
00:01:33,064 --> 00:01:36,673
Execution uses a separate interpreter with resource
limits.

21
00:01:36,853 --> 00:01:39,738
The first successful call saves the generated tool.

22
00:01:39,918 --> 00:01:42,728
Saved tools return to the registry on startup.

23
00:01:43,967 --> 00:01:47,622
Twenty five times four is the command line's default
example.

24
00:01:47,802 --> 00:01:53,953
The calculator parses a syntax tree, accepts arithmetic
nodes, and evaluates multiplication.

25
00:01:54,133 --> 00:01:58,388
Its text result, one hundred, returns as a function call
output.

26
00:01:58,568 --> 00:02:02,183
The client adds that output to the model context for the
next step.

27
00:02:03,417 --> 00:02:06,949
With at least two agents, up to five propose answers and
vote.

28
00:02:07,129 --> 00:02:11,499
Anonymous voting hides authors and shuffles candidate
order for each voter.

29
00:02:11,679 --> 00:02:15,727
Plurality selects the answer, with ties following the
earliest ballot.

30
00:02:15,907 --> 00:02:20,572
Identified mode shows authors and a live tally as agents
vote in sequence.

31
00:02:21,817 --> 00:02:25,453
The reviewer receives worker outputs and the chosen
candidate.

32
00:02:25,633 --> 00:02:29,672
It can request follow up tasks, returning execution to the
scheduler.

33
00:02:29,852 --> 00:02:36,227
Refinement uses a reviewer score threshold of eight, a
score gain threshold of one, and up to three rounds.

34
00:02:36,407 --> 00:02:40,829
The loop also finishes when there are no new tasks,
returning the answer text.

35
00:02:42,067 --> 00:02:45,342
SQLite retains plans and generated tool code.

36
00:02:45,522 --> 00:02:49,367
Plans with a reviewer score of at least eight are stored
after execution.

37
00:02:49,547 --> 00:02:54,834
Keyword search retrieves up to two matching plans with
scores of at least seven for the coordinator.

38
00:02:55,014 --> 00:02:57,715
Saved tools load into the registry on startup.

39
00:02:57,895 --> 00:03:02,272
The four most recent chat turns supply session context for
the next question.

40
00:03:03,517 --> 00:03:08,225
DynaAgent connects task specific workers and tools through
a dependency graph.

41
00:03:08,405 --> 00:03:14,083
Optional voting and review guide the answer, while memory
carries plans and tools between runs.

42
00:03:14,263 --> 00:03:19,741
The interface returns the final answer and exposes the
workflow through execution events.
